  * Fix handle_mode (ServerChannelOps.cpp:280) edge cases (verified by tester scenario 54):

| # | Edge Case | Input Example | Current Flawed Behavior | Expected / Standard Behavior |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **1** | Missing sign on unknown mode | `MODE #chan x` | Silently dropped with no reply (`sign == 0`) | Emit `472 <nick> x :is unknown mode char to me` |
| **2** | Ban query syntax | `MODE #chan +b` | Emits `472` (only bare `b` handled) | Return `368 <nick> <chan> :End of Channel Ban List` |
| **3** | Duplicate mode flags | `MODE #chan +ii` | Broadcasts `:Nick MODE #chan +ii` | Normalize to `:Nick MODE #chan +i` in broadcast |
| **4** | Net-zero / self-cancelling modes | `MODE #chan +t-t` | Broadcasts `:Nick MODE #chan +t-t` | Suppress broadcast when net state change is empty |
| **5** | Parameter starvation / skew | `MODE #chan +ko Bob` | Steals `Bob` as `+k` key; `+o` fails with `461` | Do not misassociate params / atomically reject or validate |
| **6** | Non-channel target | `MODE Alice` | Silently ignored (`channel_name[0] != '#'`) | Handle user mode query or return `403`/`502` |



